# GNO toolkit (always)

Human source of truth: `GNO/projects/TOOLKIT.md`. Follow it for every tool under `GNO/projects/`.

## Layout

- One tool = one folder + own git repo, `.env`, Supabase ports.
- `apps/api` (Nest) + `apps/web` (Vite React) + `supabase/migrations` + `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- HTTP feature modules: `controller` + `service` + `dto/` + optional `rules.ts` / `types.ts`.
- Internal data modules (e.g. `ads/`): **no controller**; export `*Service` only; repository private.
- Controllers stay thin — **no inline DTO classes**.

## Request path

`HTTP → DTO → service → rules (pure) + repository/data service`

- No business math in controllers or repositories.
- `rules.ts` has no Nest, Supabase, or `fs`.

## Defaults

Named constants (`DEFAULT_*`, page sizes) in `types.ts` / `shared/constants.ts` — not magic numbers in JSX or services.

## Docs

Update `README.md` + `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` in the same change as structure or operator-flow changes.

## Checks

`pnpm test` and `pnpm typecheck` before calling work done.
